--- !u!114 &1175212518
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1175212516}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Historically, gold prospecting played a major role in shaping cultures
    and economies around the world. Famous gold rushes in California, Alaska, and
    Australia drew thousands of fortune seekers. These rushes led to the rapid development
    of towns, transportation systems, and trade networks. Although few people today
    strike it rich, prospecting remains a meaningful link to this adventurous heritage.
    Many enjoy the sense of connection to the past as much as the hunt for gold itself.\n\n
    Modern prospectors often rely on community knowledge to improve their techniques.
    Clubs, online forums, and local groups share tips on equipment, geology, and
    promising locations. These communities provide support for beginners and foster
    collaboration among seasoned prospectors. Group outings allow participants to
    learn from one another while exploring new areas. The social aspect of prospecting
