      m_Calls: []
  m_text: ' One of the most common forms of gold encountered by prospectors is nugget
    gold, which consists of larger, naturally occurring chunks of metallic gold.
    Nuggets vary in size from tiny specks to several ounces, and they are often found
    in riverbeds or placer deposits where water has concentrated the heavier material.
    Their irregular shapes and shiny, metallic appearance make them easy to identify
    compared to surrounding rocks and sediment. '
