  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "long, channel-like device called a sluice box. Water flows through the
    box, carrying sediment across riffles designed to trap heavier particles like
    gold. Sluicing allows prospectors to process much larger quantities of material
    than panning alone. It\u2019s especially effective in areas with steady water
    flow and abundant gravel. Many experienced prospectors use sluicing to increase
    their chances of finding gold.\n\n Metal detecting is another useful tool in
    gold prospecting, particularly in areas with shallow, scattered nuggets. Modern
    detectors can identify metallic objects buried beneath soil, sand, or gravel.
    Prospectors often search dry streambeds, old mining sites, and hillsides where
    gold-bearing quartz may be present. The success of metal detecting often depends
    on choosing the right equipment and understanding local geology. With practice,
    prospectors can distinguish between trash signals and genuine gold targets."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
